      "claim": "Disopyramide aqueous solubility is 1 mg/mL, moderate yet consistent with its essentially complete absorption and human absolute F of 0.78 to 0.85.",
      "card_ids": ["C209", "C08", "C22"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 permeability and absorption records do not measure systemic F directly, but they affirm the absorption component for the query's structural class and do not provide any affirmative evidence for F below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C190", "C194"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
